## Findings

- **High — `Compact` drops user messages for supported transcript variants** (`cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact.go`)  
  The converter only accepts `type == "user"` and ignores both legacy Claude-style `type == "human"` and Cursor-style `role == "user"`. In this repo, those variants are explicitly supported elsewhere, so this would silently remove user prompts from compacted output for those transcripts.

```66:84:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact.go
func convertLine(lineBytes []byte, opts CompactOptions) [][]byte {
	var raw map[string]json.RawMessage
	if err := json.Unmarshal(lineBytes, &raw); err != nil {
		return nil
	}

	entryType := unquote(raw["type"])
	if droppedTypes[entryType] {
		return nil
	}

	switch entryType {
	case "assistant":
		return convertAssistant(raw, opts)
	case "user":
		return convertUser(raw, opts)
	default:
		return nil // drop unknown types in the new format
	}
}
```

```704:710:cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go
// - Claude Code uses "type": "human" or "type": "user"
// - Cursor uses "role": "user"
msgType, _ := entry["type"].(string)
msgRole, _ := entry["role"].(string)
isUser := msgType == "human" || msgType == "user" || msgRole == "user"
if !isUser {
	continue
}
```

- **Medium — user content is not IDE-tag sanitized in compact output** (`cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact.go`)  
  `extractUserContent` returns raw text directly; unlike existing prompt extraction code paths, it does not call `StripIDEContextTags`. This can leak bulky IDE context tags and reduce signal quality for API consumers.

```183:223:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact.go
func extractUserContent(contentRaw json.RawMessage) (string, []toolResultEntry) {
	// String content
	var str string
	if json.Unmarshal(contentRaw, &str) == nil {
		return str, nil
	}
	// ...
	return text, toolResults
}
```

```155:174:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/parse.go
if str, ok := msg.Content.(string); ok {
	return textutil.StripIDEContextTags(str)
}
// ...
if len(texts) > 0 {
	return textutil.StripIDEContextTags(strings.Join(texts, "\n\n"))
}
```

## Open Questions / Assumptions

- Assuming `Compact` is intended for general `full.jsonl` inputs across agents/sessions (not only a narrow modern Claude `type:"user"` subset).  
- If this is intentionally Claude-only, I’d still recommend enforcing that contract explicitly (validation/error) instead of silently dropping non-matching lines.

